// Grow MEDIA registry (infinite-of-X): each entry is a WAY crops are grown, matched to
// a garden machine by its id, then the Inventory garden edit modal renders the listed
// controls for it. Add a medium here (plus a machine in machines/home.ron whose id
// matches) and it appears with NO code change. First matching entry wins, so order
// matters: the exact "staple_grain_tray" is listed before the broader "_bed" suffix.
//
// Matching (any that is set is tried, exact -> prefix -> suffix):
//   match_exact:  Some("mushroom_rack")        machine id equals this
//   match_prefix: Some("aeroponic_tower")      machine id starts with this
//   match_suffix: Some("_bed")                 machine id ends with this
//
// default_crop: the plant id (data/plants.csv) the Plant button sows when the user
// hasn't typed one into the Crop field. Media without one (towers plant from their
// slot design; mushroom/aquaponic species aren't in plants.csv yet) get no button.
//
// Controls (rendered top to bottom in the edit modal):
//   Slider(key, label)  a 0..1 slider stored under `key` (water / nutrient / humidity / ...)
//                       "nutrient" runs the area's automatic feeder (2026-09-26): it tops each
//                       slot's N-P-K up from fertilizer in home storage. Half-way is just
//                       enough, lower under-feeds, higher holds a bigger reserve but grows
//                       nothing faster (crates/humanity-systems/src/farming/soil.rs, feed_target). It no
//                       longer multiplies growth speed.
//   Crop(label, hint)   a text field for the primary crop / species / fish
//   Toggle(key, label)  a checkbox stored under `key`
//
// show_slots: true draws the matching aeroponic tower's planted-slot list above the controls.
//
// plots (2026-09-26): how many plots one machine of this medium is divided into, one crop
// in each, so a bed can grow two crops or stagger its sowing. Every crop is tagged with the
// machine it stands in. A plot's floor is the machine's footprint over `plots`, unless
// `stacked: true` (shelves one above another, each with the whole footprint). Absent = 1.
// Towers ignore it: a tower cup is one plant. The plot counts are layout choices, not data
// about the crops: a 2 x 1 m bed or tray is two 1 m2 plots, a 2.4 x 2.4 m field four
// 1.44 m2 plots (square-metre plots, the way a garden plan is drawn).
//
// takes (2026-10-12, first-hour audit F11): what a seed from the backpack may be sown
// into (its Plant button sows into the nearest free place within reach,
// crates/humanity-systems/src/farming/sowing.rs). Plants (the default when absent): every green plant.
// Fungi: a mushroom's spawn and nothing green (the rack's shelves are in the dark of its
// tent). NoSeeds: nothing (a fish tank).
(
    media: [
        (
            id: "aeroponic",
            match_prefix: Some("aeroponic_tower"),
            label: "Aeroponic tower - sun-lit, soil-less",
            note: "Roots hang in air, misted with nutrient water; the canopy lives under the skylight. Light, not floor area, is the cap.",
            show_slots: true,
            controls: [
                Slider(key: "water", label: "Mist water"),
                Slider(key: "nutrient", label: "Nutrient feed (half is enough)"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            id: "grain_tray",
            match_exact: Some("staple_grain_tray"),
            label: "Grain tray - shallow staple tray",
            note: "Shallow trays for cereals. Cereal is the worst per-m2 indoor crop, so these are deliberately few.",
            default_crop: Some("wheat"),
            plots: 2,
            controls: [
                Crop(label: "Grain", hint: "e.g. wheat"),
                Slider(key: "water", label: "Soil moisture"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            id: "oilseed_bed",
            match_exact: Some("oilseed_bed"),
            label: "Oilseed bed - oil crops",
            note: "Sunflower and other oil crops. Cooking fat is the hardest calorie to grow indoors.",
            default_crop: Some("sunflower"),
            plots: 2,
            controls: [
                Crop(label: "Oil crop", hint: "e.g. sunflower"),
                Slider(key: "water", label: "Soil moisture"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            id: "soil_bed",
            match_suffix: Some("_bed"),
            label: "Soil bed - deep in-ground substrate",
            note: "A deep bed for root + bulk crops. Carries the real calories the towers cannot.",
            default_crop: Some("potato"),
            plots: 2,
            controls: [
                Crop(label: "Primary crop", hint: "e.g. potato"),
                Slider(key: "water", label: "Soil moisture"),
                Toggle(key: "amend", label: "Compost amendment"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            id: "mushroom",
            match_exact: Some("mushroom_rack"),
            label: "Mushroom rack - no light needed",
            note: "Uses the dark vertical space the canopy cannot. Substrate + humidity, no sun.",
            // Five shelves in a 1.8 m rack, 36 cm apart, two fruiting blocks on
            // each: the ten blocks its tent holds (2026-09-27; was four shelves).
            // oyster_mushroom's area_per_plant_m2 of 0.36 m2 is half a shelf, so
            // the model's plants per shelf are the tent's blocks. A layout
            // choice; data/garden/yields.ron (MUSHROOMS, THE RACK) says why.
            plots: 5,
            stacked: true,
            // Each rack fruits inside its own tent (2026-09-26): the rack's
            // 1.2 x 1.8 x 0.6 m shelving wrapped in clear plastic, 5 cm clear
            // of it all round, holding ten 5 lb (2.27 kg) fruiting blocks.
            // data/garden/humidity.ron (THE FRUITING TENT) has the sources and
            // the fresh air this much substrate needs.
            enclosure: Some((
                size: (1.3, 1.9, 0.7),
                substrate_kg: 22.7,
                // THE COVER (2026-11-13, engine::fruiting_tent draws it from the rack's frame).
                // The operator, 2026-11-10, on the racks: "Do you see how the shelving looks
                // like it's kind of encased in tinted glass?" It was five flat quads in the
                // glass material. What a real one is, from the pages read 2026-11-13 (each
                // site's robots.txt read first):
                //   North Spore, "How to Make a Martha Tent Mushroom Fruiting Chamber"
                //     (northspore.com/blogs/the-black-trumpet, dated 2021-11-11): a
                //     "transparent tent", a "clear plastic cover" over metal wire shelving,
                //     five shelves recommended, the fresh air "fan will sit at the top", an
                //     optional "4 inch Ducting" for its exhaust, the humidifier at the bottom,
                //     the tent standing on a drip tray.
                //   GroCycle, "How To Build a Martha Grow Tent" (grocycle.com, published
                //     2022-05-30, modified 2026-03-13): a "clear plastic zip-up cover"; the fan
                //     on the top shelf, its hole traced and cut "slightly smaller than the
                //     inside of the exhaust", its filter held by a 4-inch hose clamp; the
                //     humidifier's wiring fed "out under the bottom of the plastic sheeting".
                //   Zamnesia, "How To Build A Martha Fruiting Chamber For Mushrooms" (dated
                //     2022-04-19): the humidifier hose through the cover's wall, the hole cut
                //     "as small as possible" and sealed.
                //   Could not read: North Spore's BoomRoom II product pages (HTTP 429 every
                //     time), whose listing describes a double zipper door panel that rolls up.
                // The rest is the common mini greenhouse cover these tents are: a door panel
                // hanging from the top seam, zipped down both sides, rolled up and tied off at
                // the top with two straps. GAME CHOICES where no page gave a number: the film's
                // look (a clear PVC cover in use is hazed and fogged with condensation, so a
                // milky sheet that hides the shelves' detail but not their shapes), its 1.5 cm
                // welded seams, how much it bows and the fold lines from its packet.
                cover: (
                    // Near-white and neutral; half opaque face-on (milkier at a slant); matte;
                    // passing on 65% of what falls on its far side, scattered.
                    film: (color: (0.86, 0.88, 0.88), alpha: 0.5, roughness: 0.55, transmission: 0.65),
                    seam_m: 0.015,
                    seam_alpha: 0.62,
                    // Held out at the corners and at each shelf (the frame), bowing 1.5 cm in
                    // between, inside the 5 cm the tent stands off the rack; the top sags 2.5 cm.
                    sag_m: 0.015,
                    top_sag_m: 0.025,
                    // Folded into a packet about a third of a metre across; each fold a soft
                    // 4 cm ridge or valley 5 mm deep, whitened along its middle.
                    crease_m: 0.005,
                    crease_pitch_m: 0.32,
                    crease_width_m: 0.04,
                    crease_white: 0.35,
                    door: (
                        face: Front,
                        zip_inset_m: 0.05,
                        zip_width_m: 0.025,
                        // A loose roll: a 2 cm core, 2.5 mm a turn (about 8.5 cm across when
                        // the whole door is rolled up).
                        roll_core_m: 0.02,
                        roll_layer_m: 0.0025,
                        roll_s: 3.0,
                        tend_reach_m: 2.0,
                        ties: 2,
                        tie_width_m: 0.025,
                        tie_m: 0.35,
                    ),
                    ports: [
                        // The CO2 fan's exhaust (it sits on top of the rack, data/machines
                        // home.ron "Tent CO2 fan"): a 4 inch (10.2 cm) sleeve high on the
                        // right side, tied off until a duct is pushed in.
                        (kind: Sleeve, face: Right, at: (0.5, 0.92), radius_m: 0.0508, length_m: 0.16),
                        // The tent humidifier's refill tubing (it stands on the bottom shelf and
                        // refills from the irrigation line, data/garden/humidity.ron): a grommet
                        // low on the left side, a 1/4 inch tube out of it and down.
                        (kind: Grommet, face: Left, at: (0.5, 0.07), radius_m: 0.0048, length_m: 0.3),
                    ],
                    fittings_color: (0.82, 0.83, 0.82),
                ),
            )),
            takes: Fungi,
            // No humidity slider: the tent's humidifier holds the air at its
            // setpoint (farming::humidity), so a slider here would do nothing
            // (2026-09-26 review found it read by nothing).
            controls: [
                Crop(label: "Species", hint: "e.g. oyster"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            id: "aquaponic",
            match_exact: Some("aquaponic_tank"),
            label: "Aquaponic tank - fish + plants",
            note: "Fish waste fertilizes the plants; the plants clean the water. Its fish give about half of one person's B12 at this yield, and omega-3: the gaps no plant fills.",
            takes: NoSeeds,
            controls: [
                Crop(label: "Fish", hint: "e.g. tilapia"),
                Slider(key: "nutrient", label: "Feed rate"),
            ],
        ),
        // The legume, tuber and oilseed fields sow their own crop (2026-09-26
        // review: every field matched the generic entry below and its Plant
        // button sowed wheat, while its card counted bean, potato or
        // sunflower). They come first because the first matching entry wins.
        (
            id: "legume_field",
            match_exact: Some("legume_field"),
            label: "Legume field - outdoor pulses, fixes its own nitrogen",
            note: "Carries the bulk calories no indoor canopy can. The silo buffers the winter.",
            default_crop: Some("bean"),
            plots: 4,
            controls: [
                Crop(label: "Crop", hint: "e.g. bean"),
                Slider(key: "water", label: "Irrigation"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            id: "tuber_field",
            match_exact: Some("tuber_field"),
            label: "Tuber field - outdoor potatoes and roots",
            note: "Carries the bulk calories no indoor canopy can. The silo buffers the winter.",
            default_crop: Some("potato"),
            plots: 4,
            controls: [
                Crop(label: "Crop", hint: "e.g. potato"),
                Slider(key: "water", label: "Irrigation"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            id: "oilseed_field",
            match_exact: Some("oilseed_field"),
            label: "Oilseed field - outdoor oil crops",
            note: "Carries the bulk calories no indoor canopy can. The silo buffers the winter.",
            default_crop: Some("sunflower"),
            plots: 4,
            controls: [
                Crop(label: "Crop", hint: "e.g. sunflower"),
                Slider(key: "water", label: "Irrigation"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            id: "field",
            match_suffix: Some("_field"),
            label: "Field crop - outdoor sun-lit, large scale",
            note: "Carries the bulk calories no indoor canopy can. The silo buffers the winter.",
            default_crop: Some("wheat"),
            plots: 4,
            controls: [
                Crop(label: "Crop", hint: "e.g. wheat"),
                Slider(key: "water", label: "Irrigation"),
            ],
        ),
    ],
)
